.TH WMMENUD 1 "wm-desktop" "wm-desktop" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
wmmenud \- keep a Window Maker menu in sync with installed applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wmmenud
[\-o \fIout\fR] [\-t "\fIterm \-e\fR"] [\-T \fItemplate\fR] [\-\-apps\-only] [\-\-dir \fID\fR] [\-\-once]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Watches every applications directory (with inotify), waits for a burst of changes to settle, regenerates the menu and
replaces the output file atomically. With \fB\-\-once\fR it writes the menu once and exits. A template lets you keep your
own entries and put the generated applications where you want them.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-apps\-only\fR
Write only the ("Applications", ...) submenu, by default to \fI~/.config/wm-desktop/applications.menu\fR, instead of a
whole root menu. Use it when you keep your own root menu (for example with WPrefs) and want just the generated
applications inside it, as an external submenu:
.br
(Applications, OPEN_MENU, "~/.config/wm-desktop/applications.menu")
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wmapps (1),
.BR wm-autostart (1)
